{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many Somerville homes have inadequate downspouts. Older properties may have original downspouts that are damaged or undersized. Rural homes sometimes have downspouts that were added piecemeal over the years without a coherent plan.</p>

<p>The result is water pooling near foundations. On clay soil, that water doesn't absorb — it spreads and persists.</p>

<p>We're just 15 minutes away and can assess your property quickly. We'll tell you exactly what you need.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>A good downspout system has three components: adequate capacity, proper positioning, and effective water dispersal.</p>

<p>For rural Somerville properties, water dispersal is often the biggest challenge. Surface extensions only move water a few feet. Underground drains can route it much farther.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We're based in Hartselle and understand rural Morgan County properties. We'll help you find the right solution — whether that's simple extensions or a more comprehensive drainage system.</p>
